# fixedbugs, defect 2389, 2026-11-09.
#
# SYMPTOM: a header defining `#define h0_p 0`, the name the C this compiler
# writes gives a function's first local when it is `p`, was *internal error*
# at exit 2: the reader knew the emitter's `f_<field>` and `t<N>` and not
# its locals' `h<N>_<name>`.
#
# FIX: panel 214's R3 reads the first note under the error that expands a
# macro, wherever it stands (`cli/own_names.hero`, `met`), and the emitter's
# names of a body are among its forms, so the header is told at exit 1.

extern "fixedbugs-2389-a-header-s-macro-meeting-the-name-of-a-local-is-told.h"  #~ ffi_header_refused
    function plus(x: i64, y: i64) -> i64

function main()
    p = 40
    print(plus(x: p, y: 2))
